# GitHub reads this for its "Cite this repository" button, Zenodo when it
# archives a release. It cites the explorer; the engine and EXIOBASE have
# their own citations (see README.md and docs/precompute.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "RaMa-Scene Explorer"
abstract: >-
  A static, map-first explorer of the greenhouse-gas emissions, jobs and
  metal-ore extraction embodied in each country's final demand, split by 15
  industry sections, over precomputed RaMa-Scene engine runs on EXIOBASE
  v3.3.sm (base year 2011): the baseline, three named interventions and 150
  material-efficiency scenarios. Flows are drawn on a flat map or a globe, and
  What if… shows how each run changes them. Every precomputed number comes from
  a verified engine run, with its provenance and checks on the same page. An
  optional live mode sends a custom scenario to the RaMa-Scene job API and
  shows its result, marked as not checked. Releases carry build provenance.
  Nothing is a forecast.
version: 0.4.0
